<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Fidelity Bank hikes half yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Fidelity Bank hikes half yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended March 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    98.2	    vs 75.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    26.0	    vs 21.0</p>
<p>    Net income		   21.70	   vs 16.01</p>
<p>    Net interest income	50.88	   vs 44.03</p>
<p>    Other income		 8.38	    vs 7.29</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 10.73	   vs 7.27</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			29.34	   vs 24.16</p>
<p>    Tax			    7.64	    vs 8.14</p>
<p>Div payable June 4</p>
<p>On register May 16</p>
<p>Full name: Fidelity Bank Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said advances are expected to grow at a similar pace in the second half of the year, despite the anticipated economic slowdown.</p>
<p>As is normal, an improvement in results is likely to be more marked in the second half of the year than in the first due mainly to expenditure patterns.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
